# Test messages of Apache James mime4j, https://github.com/apache/james-mime4j at commit c2198afe29a738af7b10ead64f2357998eed7d8b,
# copied byte for byte with curl on 2026-09-27, each from the source URL followed by its path. The build verifies each file against
# its SHA-256 and fails on a mismatch, a missing file or an unlisted one (project/VendoredFiles.scala).
#
# For each message X.msg: X_decoded.xml, mime4j's part tree with each entity's raw header fields, and X_decoded_<path>.txt or .bin,
# each leaf after transfer decoding, named by the xml's text-body and binary-body elements. These are another parser's reading,
# compared with the module's, never taken as truth. Every file was read before vendoring; the messages are synthetic (example
# domains, test phrases, RFC quotations).
#
# Excluded:
#   example.msg and its goldens: a real delivered message; its trace fields carry a person's name, personal addresses and network
#   addresses, though its body is test text.
#   missing-inner-boundary_decoded_1_2_1.txt, multipartemptypart_decoded_1_2.txt, multipartnestedemptyparts_decoded_1_1.txt: named
#   by no _decoded.xml, so no golden refers to them.
#   The X.xml event streams and X.out writer outputs: the tests compare trees and decoded leaves only.
#
